+// S03-T04: ALife activation and awareness for both participants, headless.
+//
+// Runs after the two-actor fixture (S03-T03), which leaves participant 2
+// holding a live actor beside actor 1. The switch rules now measure from the
+// nearest alive participant actor (CALifeSwitchManager::activation_distance);
+// the fixture checks that rule on the running level, phase by phase:
+//
+//  1 baseline:   settle (no switch for quiet_ticks), then every object on the
+//                level satisfies the switch rule against the activation
+//                anchors; the anchors are the two actors' server entities;
+//                250 ticks are measured (tick wall time, online count, object
+//                and scheduler updates, level frame timing); the cost of the
+//                distance rule itself is measured over the registry.
+//  2 separate:   actor 2 is teleported (as CScriptGameObject::SetActorPosition
+//                does) to the farthest accessible level vertex from actor 1;
+//                after the settle the rule holds again; objects near actor 2
+//                and beyond the offline distance of actor 1 came online;
+//                nothing near actor 1 went offline; 250 ticks are measured.
+//  3 awareness:  god mode on; a monster spawned beside each actor comes online
+//                and takes its own actor as its enemy; both are released.
+//  4 disconnect: participant 2's session detaches; its retained actor still
+//                anchors its area, the level and ALife go on; it re-attaches.
+//  5 return:     actor 2 goes back beside actor 1; the objects that came
+//                online for actor 2 alone go offline again; the rule holds.
+//
+// If the level cannot separate the actors by more than the offline distance
+// plus a margin, the switch distance is lowered for the fixture only (or set
+// with -s03-switch-distance <m>) and restored at the end.
+//
+// CSV rows (s03-t04-activation.csv):
+//   meta,<frame>,<level>,<actor1>,<actor2>,<monster_section>,<switch_distance>,<online_distance>,<offline_distance>
+//   tick,<tick>,<phase>,<step>,<engine_us>,<online>,<switched_on>,<switched_off>,<anchors>,<from_participants>,
+//        <object_updates>,<scheduler_updates>
+//   switch,<tick>,<phase>,<id>,<name>,<online|offline>,<d1>,<d2>
+//   rule,<phase>,<modelled>,<unmodelled>,<online>,<violations>
+//   violation,<phase>,<id>,<name>,<online>,<can_on>,<can_off>,<distance>
+//   separation,<distance>,<vertex>,<x>,<y>,<z>,<switch_distance>,<online_distance>,<offline_distance>
+//   window,<name>,<ticks>,<engine_us_per_tick>,<online_mean>,<object_updates>,<scheduler_updates>,
+//          <objects_update_ms>,<game_events_ms>,<script_ms>
+//   bench,<objects>,<reps>,<alife_actor_ns>,<activation_ns>,<refresh_ns>
+//   aware,<label>,<tick>,<monster>,<actor>,<distance>,<feel_distance>,<alive>,<visible_for_ai>,<relation_enemy>,
+//         <relation_type>,<vertex_ok>,<vertex>,<useful>,<vision_enabled>,<traced_count>,<traced>,<fuzzy>,<raw_count>,
+//         <raw>,<value>,<threshold>,<always_visible>,<luminocity>,<not_yet_visible>,<visual_count>,<in_visual>,
+//         <seen_now>,<enemies>,<in_enemies>,<enemy>,<precache_frame>,<ignore_actor>
+//         (or aware,<label>,<tick>,<monster>,<actor>,<distance>,dead)
+//   check,<phase>,<ok>,<what>
+//   end,<ticks>,<sim_ms>,<wall_ms>,<checks>,<failures>,<phase>,<ok>
